   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE** — head 35cd228d81a0daa3b2764254e0b53ce2b8a517bb\n\nNothing blocks the merge. Four non-blocking findings:\n\n1. **Low**, `TopicListView.swift:74-78`. Legacy always shows \"+\" and greys it out when logged out or without a new-topic URL (`.disabled(!isLoggedIn || viewModel.newTopicURL == nil)`, `MainWindow.swift:842` @ 87fe0d1c). SwiftHFR hides it. Kept on purpose, but the file header did not list it as a difference (AGENTS.md §4). Fix: add it to the header's \"Differences\".\n2. **Low**, `TopicListView.swift:80`. Legacy plays `AppHaptics.refreshStarted()` on refresh (`MainWindow.swift:382`). SwiftHFR has no haptics caller yet. Fix: add \"no haptic\" to the header's \"Differences\".\n3. **Detail**, `RootTabsView.swift:72`. The Favoris tab also gets the refresh button, next to its `.primaryAction` `FavoritesSourceMenu`; this matches legacy (`Favorites.swift:798-806`). The PR should say so.\n4. **Detail**, PR body. \"Fails without the change (`canRefresh` does not exist)\" is a compile failure; the test does go red with `canRefresh { true }` (`[true, true]` vs `[false, false]`). Say that.\n\nVerified: diff vs `origin/dev-swift` and legacy `MainWindow.swift:375-393`, `:828-851`, `Common.swift:388-404`, `Favorites.swift:798-806`; SwiftLint clean on the 3 files; `ToolbarContentBuilder`, `symbolEffect(.rotate, options: .repeating, isActive:)`, `@Sendable` capture of the `@MainActor` model and local `Mutex` checked by reading. Not run: app build and tests (CI and Mac checks needed).\n\nAuthor: findings 1 and 2 fixed in the pointer comment (one commit); 3 and 4 fixed in the PR body.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
